          "path": ".github/scripts/authz_gauntlet_checks.py",
          "line": 46,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "bug",
          "title": "Keep index predicate matching within its SQL statement",
          "body": "The `.*?` before `WHERE` crosses semicolons. For example, `CREATE INDEX ix ON t (a); DELETE FROM t WHERE created_at < now()` matches the DELETE predicate and reports an invalid index, although the index has no predicate and the cleanup is valid. Since findings block merge, this rejects valid migrations on firing PRs. Restrict this portion of the match to the current statement and add a regression test for this multi-statement SQL.",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "source_pass": "main"
        },
        {
          "path": ".github/workflows/authz-gauntlet-panel.yml",
          "line": 274,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "security",
          "title": "Git permissions allow overwriting the trusted extractor",
          "body": "These unrestricted Git arguments bypass the read-only boundary: `git log -1 --format=%B --output=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/authz-gauntlet-trusted/panel_comment.py\" HEAD` writes the PR commit body over the pinned extractor. The later extraction step explicitly executes that file with Python. A prompt-injected reviewer can therefore turn attacker-controlled commit text into execution in this OIDC-enabled job, despite `Write` and `Edit` being denied. Git documents this file-writing option in its [log reference](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-log). Enforce read-only access outside the model's permission rules, or expose trusted wrappers that validate arguments and reject output-file options.",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "source_pass": "main"
        }
      ],
