      "comments": [
        {
          "path": "scripts/cleanup_ccc_backlog.py",
          "line": 114,
          "severity": "BLOCKER",
          "category": "bug",
          "title": "Recheck lead eligibility before dismissing snapshot rows",
          "body": "These live checks do not detect qualification or other decisions since the refresh. An old, quiet lead qualified after the nightly refresh still has `deleted_at IS NULL` and `is_dismissed = false`, so `_DISMISS_LEADS` sets `is_dismissed = true` on that qualified deal. The freshness guard permits snapshots up to 36 hours old, making this possible during ordinary use. Recheck the current candidate predicate in the update's selection so cleanup cannot dismiss a deal that has already left the pre-qualified population.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "source_pass": "main"
        },
        {
          "path": "hickory-ui/backend/app/services/ccc_worklist.py",
          "line": 2950,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "bug",
          "title": "Reprobe clearing history when an open contact changes identity",
          "body": "`_build_open_contact_rows` replaces the stored identity with the live contact's identity, but this probe condition only considers refresh age. For example, a 40-day-old open contact reassigned after today's refresh to a person reached 20 days ago still reads unanswered on the 14-day list: that person's reply is outside the clearing window, and the refresh judged a different person. The lead arm already handles this case with `same_person` and `reprobe`. Carry an identity-change flag for contacts too and trigger the backward probe when their tenant or identity handles change.",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "source_pass": "main"
        },
        {
          "path": "hickory-ui/backend/app/services/ccc_worklist.py",
          "line": 4080,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "bug",
          "title": "Keep older triaged contacts reachable through state selection",
          "body": "The nightly replacement excludes every handled, dismissed, or currently snoozed contact here. Once an older contact is excluded, neither worklist contact arm can return it: the live arm only scans the display window, and the older arm only reads this table. Consequently, handling a 40-day-old contact makes it selectable until the next refresh, after which selecting `handled` cannot find it. This contradicts the stated behavior that every state remains reachable by selection. Provide a history path for explicit state selections while keeping the default queue restricted to open items.",
          "confidence": 0.97,
          "source_pass": "main"
        }
      ],
