          "path": "payment-portal/backend/src/routes/saved_charge.py",
          "line": 337,
          "severity": "BLOCKER",
          "category": "race-condition",
          "title": "Persist an atomic invoice claim before charging",
          "body": "All duplicate-payment checks run before `_charge`, and the first payment write happens afterward. Two staff modals can therefore both pass the DB checks and Braintree search before either creates a transaction, charging the invoice twice. The description acknowledges this race, but a per-modal lock cannot prevent it across clients. There is also no durable retry guard if Braintree loses its answer and `_record` fails: reopening the modal permits another charge during the search-lag window. Atomically reserve the invoice and environment before calling Braintree, fail closed if that reservation cannot be persisted, and retain the reservation for unknown outcomes.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "source_pass": "main"
        },
        {
          "path": "payment-portal/backend/src/routes/saved_charge.py",
          "line": 315,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "bug",
          "title": "Reject a balance change of exactly one cent",
          "body": "The `> Decimal(\"0.01\")` comparison accepts a balance change of exactly one cent. For example, a signed amount of `199.00` still charges when the portal reloads a balance of `198.99` or `199.01`. This bypasses the promised balance recheck after the staff-facing service has signed the request. Compare the amounts for equality at cent precision.",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "source_pass": "main"
        },
        {
          "path": "payment-portal/backend/src/routes/saved_charge.py",
          "line": 332,
          "severity": "WARNING",
          "category": "security",
          "title": "Concurrent requests can charge the same invoice multiple times",
          "body": "The prior-payment checks and processor search are separate from the charge, with no atomic reservation or lock. Two concurrent requests for the same invoice can both find no payment or Braintree transaction, then both call `_charge` before either records its result. A staff user with the charge capability can trigger this by submitting parallel requests; the modal lock does not protect the endpoint. Signing and expiration also do not prevent concurrent replay of a valid token. This can charge the customer's saved payment method multiple times for one invoice.",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "source_pass": "security"
        }
      ],
